         method='Use the same records and scenarios across candidates. Keep the actual edition, participant roles, and proposed integrations beside every observation so a trial result can be traced to the setup being purchased.',
         items=[('Process fit', 'Demonstrate the actual qualification, proposal, and decision steps. Avoid changing your acceptance test to match a vendor’s demonstration.'), ('Record relationships', 'Verify the contacts, companies, opportunities, activities, and history your workflow needs. An import count alone does not prove relationships survived.'), ('Ownership and coverage', 'Test assignment, backup access, and overdue next actions. An unowned inquiry remains unowned even in an attractive interface.'), ('Handoffs and exceptions', 'Run a signed deal with missing information and a failed transfer. Observe whether the receiver can accept or return it clearly.'), ('Reporting definitions', 'Reproduce an agreed pipeline sample from source records. A manager should understand what a stage total actually includes.'), ('Maintenance by your team', 'Ask the intended administrator to perform a routine change and resolve an exception. Include that operating effort in the decision.'), ('Total committed cost', 'Combine the required plan, seats, charges, migration, training, and administration. Confirm the commercial terms for the actual configuration.')],
